ut the rowdy mundane video like so  many actors today Tommy Flanagan has  made an appearance in the ever-expanding  Marvel Cinematic Universe and most  people would agree that Flanagan  supporting turnest Tolkien guardians of  the galaxy vol 2 ranks among the most  memorable  of his after Sons of Anarchy gigs if  you've already ventured into the goofy  yet surprisingly heartfelt deep space  drama of guardians of the galaxy vol 2  you'll remember Flanagan's appearance in  the film as a member of the yondu  ravager plan tulké was also one of the  most loyal members of yondu's crew which  is important to note because one of the  subplots of the film involved an all-out  mutiny among the Ravagers and those  Ravagers who remained loyal to their  captain didn't fare particularly well as  it is Flanigan's final moments in  guardians of the galaxy vol 2 also  remained some of the most unexpectedly  touching ones in the entire film while  Charlie Hunnam struggles with letting go  of Sons of Anarchy have been  well-documented since the show went off  air it's safe to say that a definite  bond of brotherhood ran through the  series cast and crew as such some of the  SAMCRO brothers have continued to appear  on screen together since Sons ended that  said Tommy Flanagan's appearance  opposite his old biker boy buddy Charlie  Hunnam in 2017 s remake of Papillon was  hardly a shocker the film based on real  events finds Hunnam genre Papillon  cherrier attempting a series of daring  prison breaks with fellow inmate Luis  daga played by Rami Malek during one of  the escapes Papillon is aided in his  endeavor by a savvy gent with a shotgun  and face full of tattoos  he's known simply as masked Breton and  he's played by hun UM's former  second-in-command Flanagan after Sons of  Anarchy Tommy Flanagan joined the ranks  of actors who've appeared in Netflix  projects  unfortunately Flanagan's Netflix run  lasted a mere ten episodes with the  short-lived wu assassins that early  cancellation was likely more algorithm  driven than anything since the show  seemed on track to become one of the  more intriguing action programmes  available on the platform still it seems  not many people actually watched those  10 episodes of Lewis asin's which means  most missed out on one of the great  Tommy Flanagan performances who's too  late the series is set in San Francisco  and finds warrior Kai Jin who's tabbed  to become the last of the titular  assassins and restore balance to the  streets of Chinatown Flanigan's crime  boss Alec McCullough is largely  responsible for the imbalance on those  streets which puts him in direct  opposition to the would be wu Hiro  Flanagan clearly had a blast breaking  bad for whoa assassins and ultimately  delivered what might have become his  signature villainous turn had more  people seen it they say you can't go  home again  but Tommy Flanagan came home to his role  of Chibs on the Sons of Anarchy spin-off  Mayans MC and he absolutely owned the  screen when he did  while many Sons of Anarchy fans fully  expected a crossover episode when series  creator Kurt Sutter announced the  spin-off that crossover didn't actually  happen until late into the show's second  season titled COO cool on the episode in  question finds the Mayans crew honoring  one of Jax tellers final request by  sitting down with the SAMCRO brothers  and hammering out details about a  lucrative deal as you can probably  imagine things don't quite go according  to plan  even so it was beyond brilliant to see  Flanagan channel his inner cribs for the  episode and were sincerely hoping Mayans  MC can find another reason to bring the  great Tommy Flanagan back for a future  episode check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more looper  videos about your favorite actors are  coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

